From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 078/112] Song browser: a group is the whole name without its
 number; groups stay open

A song's versions are grouped by the whole name without the number at its
end (and the ' ', '_', '-' or '.' before it; case doesn't matter): "New
Sitar Grii", "New Sitar Grii 2", "New Sitar Grii 9", "New Sitar Grii 10" are
the row "New Sitar Grii >"; "TRACK", "TRACK 2", "TRACK3" the row "TRACK >". A
name without a number at its end is a song of its own ("New Drum Idea",
"TRACK FINAL"), and so is the firmware's name for a new song, "SONG" and a
number ("SONG1", "SONG001"). The row shows the whole name (cut before the
arrow, scrolling when selected; 7-segment: the name and "--").

A group folded out stays so when the select encoder moves on, and several
can be folded out at once. BACK on one of a group's versions folds that
group in and selects its row; BACK anywhere else goes up a folder or exits
as before (the groups all folded in). The groups folded out are kept by
name, at most 8: folding out a 9th folds in the one the selection was in
longest ago. Entering or leaving a folder, and opening the browser, fold
them all in (on opening, a later version's group is folded out as before).

